
<p>Joe Rossignol, MacRumors:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>If you were hoping to surprise someone with an iPhone Duo for
Christmas, you might be out of luck, as Apple’s online store in
the U.S. is already showing an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/iphone-duo-preorder-shipping-wait-times/">estimated shipping date of January
25</a> for all configurations following the start of pre-orders today.</p>

<p>It is possible that some Apple Stores will have the iPhone Duo
available for walk-in customers on Friday, October 23 launch day,
but it seems likely that inventory will be very tight.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>I suspect it’s a combination of high demand and low supply but I doubt we’ll get any insight on that from Apple itself. It’s in their interest to let people think demand is simply very high, and not draw attention to their production limits.</p>

<p>I feel for the folks on the West Coast who woke up for a 5:00am start and still got stuck with December or even January ship dates. This is one of those times where it’s frustrating that, per <a href="https://daringfireball.net/2026/09/spitballing_predictions_for_apples_october">Apple’s consistent schedule</a>, pre-orders always start before reviews appear. People are left to guess whether they’re going to like it without any word from people who’ve used it.</p>

